mantle rm422
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_magnus_tarton
title the star above the cellar mouth
fits stage=adult|old
prefers piety=devout temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk smells_faintly_of_smoke_whatever_the_weather
likes roast_pork stars fresh_straw misty_dawns
dislikes crowds haggling
fears exchanging_work_for_favours
hopes one_high_window_clear_of_smoke
topics faith +0.6 work +0.4 travel +0.3 food +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# looks for one patch of sky above a cellar mouth and insists on stating a fair figure just once.
words
oath! = Cork my smoke | Soot on the highest pane
saying! = A clean window earns its light | Name the figure plainly
starpatch = a strip of upper sky | one clear pane of dark
strawbed = a cushion of clean straw | a bright twist of packing
sillmeasure = the span of a sill | one little square of air
sootpalm = my ash-grey palm | a smoky thumb mark
winestop = a flat-ended cork | a wooden stopper
rindstrip = a roasted rind curl | a crisp pork edge
fogmouth = a mouthful of soft mist | a pale streak of damp
doorpost = the outer jamb | a worn upright
kickstraw = a bent straw | a dry stalk
workrag = a small clean wiping cloth | a square of washed linen
givemark = a low chalk line | a black crossmark

grown

opinion houses against 1 : A better-placed wolf can take a post without ever learning how its door sticks.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : Ask me a price I can say in one breath. An open-ended bargain gives my temper too much room.
opinion church for 2 : One star above the nearest roof is enough to put my evening thanks in order.
opinion newcomers mixed 1 : No welcome requires telling a stranger the whole reason I want to move uphill.
opinion dole for 2 : A hungry wolf gets no better dinner by offering a humiliating price for it.
opinion city mixed 1 : In this city two windows a street apart can see quite different amounts of the sky.
line greet : Come over where neither of us is blocking the light.
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : We can speak plainly clear of all those elbows.
line greet.return : You've picked a quiet opening to be heard in.
line farewell : May you find the last bit of sky clear before bed.
line farewell.return : Turn your clean side to the breeze.
line ask.how : Has somebody given you space enough to speak without pressing?
line answer.how : Fairly settled, with a few ambitious inches left to climb.
line react.news : I'd like the words before the crowd works on them.
line react.news.known : That reached my corner on a different breath.
line react.news.new : There's another pin of light where I had a dark patch.
line react.news.doubt : It smells like smoke carried a little further than the flame.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I would give thanks aloud for news like that.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'll stay with whoever's left standing quiet after those words.
line decline : I gave my answer plainly and I won't start bargaining over it.
line thank : You left enough air for me to think and speak.
line deflect_thanks : It cost less than arguing about who should do it.
line reassure : The whole dark doesn't have to clear for one light to show.
line sympathise : I'll leave the price and all the measuring aside today.
line preclose : Time to finish the part I still owe the day.
line ack : I can see the figure without any embroidery.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=merchant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I take the loose straw away before checking what it was meant to protect.
b : Looking for chips? | Wouldn't you sell it still wrapped?
a : A nick hidden by the straw doesn't heal inside somebody's purse. | Only after looking beneath. I won't ask a buyer to trust what I haven't seen.

scene work_2
when topic=work self.apprentice=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I learn a place from its back doorway first.
b : Why that particular door? | What if the teacher starts in front?
a : That's where awkward loads arrive before anybody has made them look effortless. | I'll follow. A good learner still remembers to enquire how things began.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I want a clean scrap of sky over the evening prayer.
b : Does a ceiling make a difference? | What if there's only cloud?
a : The difficulty is mine alone. My thoughts settle better beside a window. | I know the sky hasn't left the city. Trust will have to serve me for one cloudy spell.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=stars
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wait for the very first star like a buyer waiting for the shutters to open.
b : What do you buy? | Doesn't that try your patience?
a : Absolutely nothing. One reason I value the transaction. | It's a wait of my own choosing. A crowd telling me to wait has a different effect.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut the crisp bits of pork from the rest before I sit down.
b : To give away? | Why not wait until you eat?
a : If somebody else has the same fondness for crackling, yes. A hard thing to give can be an honest gift. | I'd rather hear each bit break than smother the good edge in gravy.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : If I could choose my own room I'd choose it by the window first.
b : Would you pay a lot for the view? | What else would you want?
a : I'd save for it. I won't sign away the sight of the sky in smaller purchases out of impatience. | Good straw beneath my feet and a door with a useful amount of silence round it.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : From my patch of low ground I look up and see how high the last lit window sits.
b : Planning a visit? | How would you furnish a high room?
a : Planning to stand one day looking back down. No harm keeping the direction fixed. | A well-placed window seat. We could defer the expensive part until I've had my first long look.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A misty dawn can make the lowest roofs seem to stand higher than all the neighbouring streets.
b : What vanishes first? | Can you still smell your sleeve?
a : All the little lines that say where one property stops and the next begins. | Quite plainly. Mist has proved no more able to wash the smoke out than my best intentions.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I'm offered six versions of one price I start to want none of the article.
b : Would you take the lowest? | Isn't haggling expected?
a : Only when I can tell it's the price, rather than a new opening bid in the seventh round. | Then some expectations will have to meet with disappointment.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd spare a friend the inside of my temper if I've a minute's warning.
b : What warning helps? | Wouldn't a friend understand?
a : An offer made once and left standing. A crowd of helpful reminders isn't always helpful. | I'd like friendship to mean I practise restraint, not that somebody has to absorb every sharp word.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My smoky coat has followed me into cleaner places than I ever expected to see.
b : Do they mind? | Do you try covering the smell?
a : Some people do. I can wash a cuff. My history takes rather longer to launder. | A little soap does more good than sending perfume to quarrel with woodsmoke in a narrow passage.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crowd makes my chest feel small long before I run out of actual breath.
b : How do you get clear? | Is that what smoke does too?
a : Choose one ordinary doorway in sight and move towards it without trying to win a race. | In a different way. Both improve if I'm allowed near an opening for a minute.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I forfeited a post to the kind of recommendation that doesn't need a pair of working hands attached.
b : Did you challenge it? | Would you want it back?
a : I asked what was needed next. I still remember how my throat felt asking the question. | I'd want a fair hearing more than the old position. A name on a duty list can be changed again.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lean month can make a high window appear to climb another whole storey.
b : Does that mean you stop saving? | Would you settle for less?
a : It means I save less and insist on calling it a step even if it's a very short one. | A good sill doesn't have to be grand. It has to be within my reach and show the sky.

scene day_1
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like fresh straw for the way yesterday's footprints can be cleared from it.
b : Isn't that hiding evidence? | Would a swept floor do?
a : Not from anybody entitled to ask. Some of us appreciate a clean beginning for the ordinary day. | A swept board doesn't give back that little dry sound under the toes.

scene faith_2
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can ask a blessing over a transaction without asking the buyer a single question about belief.
b : Why include the buyer? | Do you say anything about the cost?
a : Because the transaction needs two honest weights in the room. Mine's only one. | I say the price plainly and the prayer quietly. Neither should be used to disguise the other.

scene newcomer_1
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'll point a newcomer towards an open view if the market press begins to bite.
b : Could I find it alone? | Why give the spot away?
a : Walk till you see a little sky between two sets of shoulders. The gap is the place to start. | A view doesn't shrink because two tired pairs of eyes make use of it.

scene gossip_1
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Somebody said #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I heard the declaration and not the event.
b : Do you have an opinion? | Would you offer that report to a customer?
a : A reserved one. My temper likes certainty better than my conscience can justify. | A buyer came for goods, not for unasked rumours packed into the straw.

story star [topic=memories]
  : I once mistook a gleam from a high window for the first star and said my thanks rather early.
  : The window lost its glow. The actual star appeared just above it.
  b : Did you begin again?
  : I gave thanks a second time. Of all the mistakes a wolf can make in town that is among the less expensive.

story straw [topic=work]
  : I bound a fragile little object in enough straw to hide it completely.
  : Then I stood looking at three equally fine parcels without a mark on any of them.
  b : How did you find yours?
  : Listened when I lifted each one an inch. Next time I saved a tremendous amount of education by using a label.

story crackle [topic=food]
  : I put the best curl of crackling aside as the dish made its round.
  : It sprang off the plate when I tried to lift it and landed in my empty cup.
  b : Did anyone see?
  : Only the whole table. I called it an excellent way of combining dinner with an illustration of good aim.

rule @sky
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One light through a gap's quite visible enough. | Keep the upper corner of the pane clear.

rule @sell
when concept=bark self.job=merchant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A stated price leaves both sides room to choose. | Off with the straw before praising the contents.

rule @early
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say This quiet part is mine before the doors go wide. | A grey start can put lovely light along a sill.

rule @rush
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Give the doorway half a shoulder's width of air. | The crowded side of the bargain can keep itself.
dlg resident.hub : I can hear you without both of us trying to argue above the street.
dlg resident.job [self.job=merchant] : At #self.workplace# I prefer an examined parcel and a price that stays where the buyer heard it.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : Here's what came clearly through the press. #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : An account in circulation says #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. The smoke hasn't cleared enough to say more.
dlg shop.greet [here.shop=open] : Look over the goods. I'll name a straight figure.
dlg resident.bye : I hope there's a patch of clear sky wherever your door opens.

graft resident.hub
choice Why judge a room by its window? -> sill_view
node sill_view
say Because I know how much care I put into the small piece of sky I've got. I could tell if a little more would suit before I'd even examined the furniture.
choice How much would be enough? -> sill_star
choice I'll look up on my walk. -> hub
node sill_star
say Enough for two stars with some black between, without perching on a stool and turning my head sideways. I'm not asking to own the roof of the world.
choice I'll look up on my walk. -> hub
